<h1>Layer Decision: &lt;service-name&gt;</h1>
<h2>Context</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Service:</strong> &lt;service-name&gt;</li><li><strong>Protocol mix:</strong> HTTPS, gRPC over HTTP/2</li><li><strong>Content routing:</strong> path-based (<code>/api</code>, <code>/static</code>, <code>/grpc</code>)</li><li><strong>TLS:</strong> terminate at LB (WAF + header inspection required)</li><li><strong>Anycast:</strong> no (single region for now)</li></ul>
<h2>Decision</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Choice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Layer</td><td>L7</td></tr><tr><td>TLS</td><td>terminate-at-lb</td></tr><tr><td>Features</td><td>path-routing, header-routing, waf</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Rationale</h2>
<p>Content-based routing + WAF integration cannot be expressed at L4. Anycast is not required at this SLA tier, so a single-tier L7 LB (ALB / Ingress-Nginx) is sufficient. If we expand to multi-region with 99.99% SLA, revise this decision to hybrid (Global Accelerator → ALB).</p>
<h2>Consequences</h2>
<ul><li>LB CPU sized for TLS termination + regex routing.</li><li>Backend pool sees plain HTTP (TLS terminated upstream).</li><li>WAF rule set lives at the LB, not the backend.</li></ul>
<h2>Status</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] Approved</li><li>[ ] Implemented</li></ul>
